<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN">
<HTML>
<HEAD>
  <META CONTENT="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" 0="content-type">
  <TITLE>Sufaces using jmol</TITLE>
  <META CONTENT="J. Gutow" NAME="author">
  <META CONTENT="Orbital display using jmol" NAME="description">
  <META CONTENT="Page design and layout by J. Gutow 5-2006, page written by perl script orbtohtml.pl" NAME="details">
  <META CONTENT="This page is designed to have the text and normal html edited in a standard web design" NAME="instr1">
  <META CONTENT="program.  The javascript is to control the jmol applet (see below).  It is best to use" NAME="instr2">
  <META CONTENT="the perl scripts to generate the proper java script to allow orbital display.  It is" NAME="instr3">
  <META CONTENT="important to have all the gzipped files in the same directory as the .html file.  The" NAME="instr4">
  <META CONTENT="files needed are: 1) a gzipped file with the atom coordinates, in any of the formats Jmol" NAME="instr5">
  <META CONTENT="can read. 2) a gzipped gaussian cube file for each of the orbitals to be displayed.  To" NAME="instr6">
  <META CONTENT="save loading time it seems to be better to avoid including the atom coordinates in the" NAME="instr7">
  <META CONTENT="cube files.  It is also recommended that the file names for the surfaces correspond to" NAME="instr8">
  <META CONTENT="reasonable names for the orbitals as the file names are used to generate the menu items" NAME="instr9">
  <META CONTENT="that appear in the popup menus for selecting orbitals." NAME="instr10">
  <META CONTENT="The relative path to Jmol on your server must be correct below!!" NAME="instr11">
  <SCRIPT SRC="../Applets/Java/Jmol/Jmol.js"></SCRIPT>
</HEAD>
<BODY>
<DIV STYLE="text-align: center;"><BIG><BIG><SPAN STYLE="font-weight: bold;">&lt;Replace this text with your title&gt;<BR>
</SPAN></BIG></BIG>
<DIV STYLE="text-align: left;"><BIG><BIG><SPAN STYLE="font-weight: bold;"></SPAN></BIG></BIG>&lt;Describe your
molecule and orbitals here. Don't forget to mention that there is a
live display below.&#160; The user's browser window may be too small to
display your text and the table containing the Jmol applet without
scrolling.&gt;
<BR>
<BR>
<BIG><BIG><SPAN STYLE="font-weight: bold;"></SPAN></BIG></BIG>
<TABLE BORDER="1" CELLPADDING="2" CELLSPACING="2" STYLE="width: 100%; text-align: left;">
  <TBODY>
    <TR>
      <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top;">
      <SCRIPT>
jmolInitialize(&quot;../Applets/Java/Jmol&quot;);
jmolApplet(300, &quot;load Cl_6-311++(2p,d).log.gz; spacefill 2%; background white&quot;);
 
        </SCRIPT>
      <BR>
      </TD>
      <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top;">
      <DIV STYLE="text-align: right;"> </DIV>
      <FORM>
        <DIV STYLE="text-align: right;"> </DIV>
        <TABLE BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="2" CELLSPACING="2" STYLE="width: 100%; text-align: left;">
          <TBODY>
            <TR>
              <TD COLSPAN="1" ROWSPAN="1" STYLE="vertical-align: top; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right;"><SPAN STYLE="font-weight: bold;">Orbital
1:</SPAN><BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top;">
              <SCRIPT>
		jmolMenu([
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete;','none'],
		['isosurface neg1 delete; isosurface pos1 delete; isosurface neg1 -0.06 &quot;testgrid.cube.gz&quot;; color isosurface red;isosurface pos1 0.06 &quot;testgrid.cube.gz&quot;;color isosurface blue;',&quot;3p&quot;],
		[&quot;&quot;, &quot;dummy&quot;]
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;">Surface
Type:<BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;">
              <SCRIPT>
		jmolRadioGroup([['isosurface neg1 fill nomesh nodots; isosurface pos1 fill nomesh nodots;','Solid','true'],
		['isosurface neg1 mesh nofill nodots; isosurface pos1 mesh nofill nodots;', 'Mesh'],
		['isosurface neg1 dots nomesh nofill; isosurface pos1 dots nomesh nofill;', 'Dot']
		 ]);

		</SCRIPT><BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;">Surface
Color:<BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;">
              <SCRIPT>
		jmolRadioGroup([['isosurface neg1; color isosurface red; isosurface pos1; color isosurface blue;',&quot;blue/red&quot;, 'true'],
		['isosurface neg1; color isosurface yellow; isosurface pos1; color isosurface green;',&quot;green/yellow&quot;],
		['isosurface neg1; color isosurface cyan; isosurface pos1; color isosurface purple;',&quot;purple/cyan&quot;],
		['isosurface neg1; color isosurface pink; isosurface pos1; color isosurface brown;',&quot;brown/pink&quot;]
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD COLSPAN="1" ROWSPAN="1" STYLE="vertical-align: top; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right;"><SPAN STYLE="font-weight: bold;">Orbital
2:</SPAN> </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top;">
              <SCRIPT>
		jmolMenu([
		['isosurface neg2 delete; isosurface pos2 delete;','none'],
		['isosurface neg2 delete; isosurface pos2 delete; isosurface neg2 -0.06 &quot;testgrid.cube.gz&quot;; color isosurface yellow;isosurface pos2 0.06 &quot;testgrid.cube.gz&quot;;color isosurface green;',&quot;3p&quot;],
		[&quot;&quot;, &quot;dummy&quot;]
		]);
</SCRIPT><BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;">Surface
Type:<BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;">
              <SCRIPT> 
		jmolRadioGroup([['isosurface neg2 fill nomesh nodots; isosurface pos2 fill nomesh nodots;','Solid','true'],
		['isosurface neg2 mesh nofill nodots; isosurface pos2 mesh nofill nodots;', 'Mesh'],
		['isosurface neg2 dots nomesh nofill; isosurface pos2 dots nomesh nofill;', 'Dot']
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;">Surface
Color:<BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;">
              <SCRIPT> 
		jmolRadioGroup([['isosurface neg2; color isosurface red; isosurface pos2; color isosurface blue;',&quot;blue/red&quot;],
		['isosurface neg2; color isosurface yellow; isosurface pos2; color isosurface green;',&quot;green/yellow&quot;, 'true'],
		['isosurface neg2; color isosurface cyan; isosurface pos2; color isosurface purple;',&quot;purple/cyan&quot;],
		['isosurface neg2; color isosurface pink; isosurface pos2; color isosurface brown;',&quot;brown/pink&quot;]
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD COLSPAN="1" ROWSPAN="1" STYLE="vertical-align: top; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right;"><SPAN STYLE="font-weight: bold;">Orbital
3:</SPAN><BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top;">
              <SCRIPT>
		jmolMenu([
		['isosurface neg3 delete; isosurface pos3 delete;','none'],
		['isosurface neg3 delete; isosurface pos3 delete; isosurface neg3 -0.06 &quot;testgrid.cube.gz&quot;; color isosurface cyan;isosurface pos3 0.06 &quot;testgrid.cube.gz&quot;;color isosurface purple;',&quot;3p&quot;],
		[&quot;&quot;, &quot;dummy&quot;]
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;">Surface
Type:<BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;">
              <SCRIPT>
	 	jmolRadioGroup([['isosurface neg3 fill nomesh nodots; isosurface pos3 fill nomesh nodots;','Solid','true'],
		['isosurface neg3 mesh nofill nodots; isosurface pos3 mesh nofill nodots;', 'Mesh'],
		['isosurface neg3 dots nomesh nofill; isosurface pos3 dots nomesh nofill;', 'Dot']
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;">Surface
Color:<BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;">
              <SCRIPT> 
		jmolRadioGroup([['isosurface neg3; color isosurface red; isosurface pos3; color isosurface blue;',&quot;blue/red&quot;],
		['isosurface neg3; color isosurface yellow; isosurface pos3; color isosurface green;',&quot;green/yellow&quot;],
		['isosurface neg3; color isosurface cyan; isosurface pos3; color isosurface purple;',&quot;purple/cyan&quot;, 'true'],
		['isosurface neg3; color isosurface pink; isosurface pos3; color isosurface brown;',&quot;brown/pink&quot;]
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD COLSPAN="1" ROWSPAN="1" STYLE="vertical-align: top; white-space: nowrap; text-align: right;"><SPAN STYLE="font-weight: bold;">Orbital
4:</SPAN><BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top;">
              <SCRIPT>
		jmolMenu([
		['isosurface neg4 delete; isosurface pos4 delete;','none'],
		['isosurface neg4 delete; isosurface pos4 delete; isosurface neg4 -0.06 &quot;testgrid.cube.gz&quot;; color isosurface pink;isosurface pos4 0.06 &quot;testgrid.cube.gz&quot;;color isosurface brown;',&quot;3p&quot;],
		[&quot;&quot;, &quot;dummy&quot;]
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;">Surface
Type:<BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;">
              <SCRIPT>
 		jmolRadioGroup([['isosurface neg4 fill nomesh nodots; isosurface pos4 fill nomesh nodots;','Solid','true'],
		['isosurface neg4 mesh nofill nodots; isosurface pos4 mesh nofill nodots;', 'Mesh'],
		['isosurface neg4 dots nomesh nofill; isosurface pos4 dots nomesh nofill;', 'Dot']
		]);

	</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
            <TR>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;">Surface
Color:<BR>
              </TD>
              <TD STYLE="vertical-align: top; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;">
              <SCRIPT> 
		jmolRadioGroup([['isosurface neg4; color isosurface red; isosurface pos4; color isosurface blue;',&quot;blue/red&quot;],
		['isosurface neg4; color isosurface yellow; isosurface pos4; color isosurface green;',&quot;green/yellow&quot;],
		['isosurface neg4; color isosurface cyan; isosurface pos4; color isosurface purple;',&quot;purple/cyan&quot;],
		['isosurface neg4; color isosurface pink; isosurface pos4; color isosurface brown;',&quot;brown/pink&quot;, 'true']
		]);

		</SCRIPT>
              <BR>
              </TD>
            </TR>
          </TBODY>
        </TABLE>
      </FORM>
      <SMALL><A HREF="http://www.java.com">Javascript</A>
for live display generated by a perl script (orbtohtml.pl) on. </SMALL><SMALL><BR>
Original
page composed by <A HREF="http://www.uwosh.edu/faculty_staff/gutow/">J.
Gutow 4/2006</A>. </SMALL> </TD>
    </TR>
    <TR>
      <TD COLSPAN="2" ROWSPAN="1" STYLE="vertical-align: top;">
      <DIV STYLE="text-align: center;"><SPAN STYLE="font-weight: bold;">Instructions
for using Jmol to display
orbitals</SPAN>: <BR>
      </DIV>
      <OL>
        <LI>Choose which orbitals to display by selecting them the
orbital popup menus.&#160; You can control orbital color and fill mode
by selecting the appropriate options following each orbital menu.&#160;

        </LI>
        <LI>ROTATE the image by
holding
down the mouse button while moving the cursor over the image.&#160;
 </LI>
        <LI>ZOOM by holding down the shift key while moving the cursor
up
(decrease magnification) or down (increase magnification) on top of the
image.&#160;
 </LI>
        <LI>Other options available in the control menu accessible by
holding
the mouse button down while the cursor is over &quot;Jmol&quot; in the lower
right corner (right click also works on a multibutton mouse).&#160;
 </LI>
        <LI>For more info about Jmol go to <A HREF="http://www.jmol.org" TARGET="_blank">www.jmol.org.</A></LI>
      </OL>
      </TD>
    </TR>
  </TBODY>
</TABLE>
</DIV>
</DIV>
</BODY>
</HTML>
